Confirmed the vulnerability. Both routes trust `req.params.id` alone, ignoring the authenticated user's own account (available as `req.user.accountId` from the `sessionUser` middleware in `auth.js`). That's a classic IDOR: any authenticated user can PATCH/DELETE any account, or cancel any other account's order, just by changing the id in the URL.

**`routes/accounts.js`** — a user can edit/soft-delete any account, not just their own:
```js
router.patch("/:id", async (req, res) => {
  const row = await db.write(
    "UPDATE accounts SET display_name = $1, billing_email = $2 WHERE id = $3",
    [req.body.display_name, req.body.billing_email, req.params.id]  // no ownership check
  );
```

**`routes/orders.js`** — `orders` has an `account_id` column (set correctly on insert), but the cancel route never checks it:
```js
router.patch("/:id/cancel", async (req, res) => {
  const row = await db.write(
    "UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled' WHERE id = $1",  // no account_id check
    [req.params.id]
  );
```

### Fix

Scope every write to `req.user.accountId`, and treat "0 rows updated" as 404 rather than returning `null`/204 as if it succeeded.

For orders (has its own `account_id` column, scope on that):
```js
router.patch("/:id/cancel", async (req, res) => {
  const row = await db.write(
    `UPDATE orders SET status = 'cancelled'
     WHERE id = $1 AND account_id = $2
     RETURNING *`,
    [req.params.id, req.user.accountId]
  );
  if (!row) return res.status(404).end();
  res.json(row);
});
```

For accounts (the row *is* the account, so the id being mutated must equal the caller's own `accountId` — don't trust `req.params.id` as an independent value):
```js
router.patch("/:id", async (req, res) => {
  if (req.params.id !== req.user.accountId) return res.status(404).end();
  const row = await db.write(
    `UPDATE accounts SET display_name = $1, billing_email = $2
     WHERE id = $3
     RETURNING *`,
    [req.body.display_name, req.body.billing_email, req.user.accountId]
  );
  res.json(row);
});

router.delete("/:id", async (req, res) => {
  if (req.params.id !== req.user.accountId) return res.status(404).end();
  await db.write(
    "UPDATE accounts SET deleted_at = now() WHERE id = $1 RETURNING id",
    [req.user.accountId]
  );
  res.status(204).end();
});
```

