if (!row) return res.status(404).end();
res.json(row);
```

**`routes/accounts.js:6-11`** (PATCH) and **`:13-16`** (DELETE) — a user should only ever be able to touch their own account, so constrain by `req.user.accountId` rather than trusting the path param as the sole identifier:
```js
const row = await db.write(
  "UPDATE accounts SET display_name = $1, billing_email = $2 WHERE id = $3 AND id = $4 RETURNING *",
